[#:seon.task{:name "changed-namespaces-flags-a-namespace-sci-merely-touched"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.sci.arm/changed-namespaces` flags a namespace SCI merely touched (an unresolved qualified symbol), so the facts stage refuses a plain call (stale-agent-platform lane; 4be90d597 hid only the diagnostic). Done when the producer no longer reports a touched-only namespace as changed and a regression evaluates a plain call over an unresolved qualified symbol."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.arm/changed-namespaces}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-def-without-line-metadata-refuses-its-origin",
            :kind :function,
            :intent
            "source-display/printer-notes.md reports (eval (read r)) defining a function without reader line metadata refused by `seon.sci.arm/write-event` output at [`:seon.batch/origin` :line]. A def without an origin must remain valid, or refusal must happen at a declared input boundary; preserve the evaluated value. Regression through SCI evaluation with positionless source form.",
            :evidence
            #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/source-display/review-printer-codex-notes.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-redefinition-in-one-pass-is-armed-with-the-earlier-contract"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A defn whose :malli/schema changes from the contract its symbol already holds (an earlier form of the same pass, or an earlier pass) is armed at its write with the EARLIER contract, so a call with the new arity in the same pass is refused: (defn ^{:malli/schema [:=> [:cat :int] :int]} h [x] (inc x)) (defn ^{:malli/schema [:=> [:cat :int :int] :int]} h [x y] (+ x y 100)) (h 1 2) answers 'refused argument count: expected a declared argument count (1)'; the next pass returns 103. Cause: `seon.sci.arm/arm!` arms under the working value's projection, which carries the earlier row's function contract, and `seon.instrument/compiled-wrapper` prefers the projection's contract and its retained compiled schema over the authored one. Correct: the write arms the contract authored at that write. Proof: seon.cluster.turn-test/a-changed-arity-redefinition-is-callable-in-the-same-pass."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.arm/arm! seon.instrument/compiled-wrapper}}
 #:seon.task{:name "arming-prints-the-authored-contract-to-read-it-back"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.sci.arm/arm!` hands `seon.sci.eval/install-function-contract!` the Var's :malli/schema as (pr-str contract), and `seon.instrument/wrap-interpreted` reads it back with edn/read-string: a value printed to text and parsed again outside the value printer (kondo's one-printer warning on arm.clj). Correct: pass the contract form as data from the write to the compile; the stored row keeps its text where the store needs it. Proof: the arming path's existing tests (seon.cluster.turn-test/a-changed-arity-redefinition-is-callable-in-the-same-pass, `seon.cluster.turn-test/contracted-redefinition-exactly-replaces-the-entity`) stay green with no pr-str on the arming path."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.arm/arm! seon.instrument/wrap-interpreted}}
 #:seon.task{:name "arming-projection-is-rebuilt-per-caller-within-one-form"
             :kind :function
             :intent "When a form registers a schema the batch has not applied yet, `seon.sci.arm/arming-projection` rebuilds the delta projection (`seon.schema/projection-with-declarations`, about 5-8 ms and 10 MB per rebuild on the default program) for each caller in that form: `seon.sci.arm/arm!` once per arming write, `seon.turn.batch/schema-notes` and `seon.turn.batch/derive-form` once each. Repro: (do (`seon.schema/register!` :k [:int]) (defn ^{:malli/schema [:=> [:cat :k] :int]} f [x] x) (defn ^{:malli/schema [:=> [:cat :k] :int]} g [x] x)). Correct: one rebuild per form whose delta changed, the value handed to every reader. Proof: a pass with that form shows one projection-with-declarations call per form in its profile, and seon.cluster.turn-test/a-function-using-a-schema-registered-in-the-same-form-is-admitted stays green."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.arm/arming-projection seon.turn.batch/derive-form}}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-unarmable-contract-breaks-the-definition"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A defn whose contract cannot arm stops working: (defn badc {:malli/schema [:=> [:cat :no.such/schema] :int]} [x] x) then (badc 1) answers 'audit.scratch/badc is unavailable: its contract did not arm' on default 2026-10-08, where plain SCI answers 1. `seon.sci.arm/arm!` catches the arming failure and replaces the Var root with refusing-root. CLAUDE.md: preserve malformed contracts as data and never arm them; the owner's law: any valid Clojure SCI can execute works. Correct: the evaluated definition keeps its root, the contract failure is a diagnostic beside it. Proof: a deftest where a defn with an unknown schema key still answers its call and the reply carries the arming diagnostic."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.arm/arm!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/repl-audit/repl-audit-opus-audit.md"}}]
